cff-version: 1.2.0
type: software
title: "A plan that fits: exploring planning constraints with a solver"
message: >-
  If you discuss or use this prototype in research or teaching, please cite
  the software and record the Git commit and geographic snapshot used.
  This citation describes software, not a published participant study.
authors:
  - name: "A plan that fits contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/akkauppi/a-plan-that-fits"
url: "https://akkauppi.github.io/a-plan-that-fits/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An exploratory browser-based planning game for understanding interacting
  spatial constraints and a solver's potential role in examining them.
  Users choose hypothetical drone-supplied parcel lockers on real walking
  geography, inspect Z3 feedback, and explore capacity and depot-outage rules.
  Learning benefits have not been evaluated in a participant study. Geographic
  data and third-party software retain their separate licences.
keywords:
  - constraint solving
  - spatial planning
  - learning
  - Z3
  - satisfiability modulo theories
  - facility location
  - geographic information systems
  - WebAssembly
